## 3. Technical Architecture (System Perspective)

### Three Layers:

**Layer 1: Control Plane** (Trusted)
- Go backend API (single binary)
- Handles auth, project CRUD, file management, K8s orchestration
- Stateless: all state in PostgreSQL or K3s API
- Runs in platform namespace on K3s

**Layer 2: Data Planes** (Untrusted)
- One Kubernetes namespace per student project environment
- Each namespace has:
  - One pod (running student's code)
  - One Service (K3s networking)
  - One Ingress rule (routes traffic to pod)
  - ResourceQuota + LimitRange (prevents resource hogging)
  - NetworkPolicy (blocks traffic to other namespaces)
  - No root privileges, limited system capabilities

**Layer 3: Storage** (External)
- PostgreSQL (metadata: users, projects, environments, sessions, deployments)
- S3 (project files, templates, build artifacts)
- Both accessed via Go backend only

### Network Flow:

```
Student Browser → Internet → EC2 Public IP → K3s Ingress Controller
                                                      ↓
                                          Ingress routes by host
                                                      ↓
                            ┌─────────────────┬─────────────────┐
                            ↓                 ↓                 ↓
                    Platform Namespace    Namespace-1       Namespace-2
                    (Go Backend, UI)    (Alice's Project)  (Bob's Project)
                            ↓                 ↓                 ↓
                        Go API Pod    Isolated App Pod   Isolated App Pod
                            ↓                 ↓                 ↓
                        PostgreSQL ← ← ← Read/Write Metadata
                        S3 ← ← ← Read/Write Files
```

